#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# box_ratios

#% text
# `box_ratios` is an option of `graphics3d` and the 3D plots: `box_ratios: [a, b, c]` gives the relative side lengths of the box.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The default for plots is `automatic`, a box with the proportions of the data; `[1, 1, 1]` draws a cube whatever the ranges are.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
graphics3d(cuboid(), box_ratios: [1, 1, 3])
#% output
#= image("box_ratios.files/box_ratios-1.svgz")

#% cell
plot3d(10*sin(x*y), [x, 0, 3], [y, 0, 3], box_ratios: [1, 1, 1])
#% output
#= image("box_ratios.files/box_ratios-2.svgz")

#% cell
plot3d(10*sin(x*y), [x, 0, 3], [y, 0, 3], box_ratios: [3, 3, 1])
#% output
#= image("box_ratios.files/box_ratios-3.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
